# An open choice is no individual for another argument (tasks.org,
# aida-referents-instantiation, 2026-10-22).  rally chooses a farmer ?u and
# owes exists y, donkey y under that choice; some_donkey chooses a donkey
# ?w of its own.  Placed under rally, some_donkey keeps ?w: the farmer is
# never taken for the donkey.  Once pedro is argued to be a donkey, the
# witness scaffold at some_donkey's choice tries pedro.
lk.
pipeline unfolded.
declare Ind : type.
declare pedro : Ind.
declare farmer : Ind -> bool.
declare donkey : Ind -> bool.
argument rally : [?u:Ind] (exists x:Ind, farmer [x] -> (exists y:Ind, donkey [y])).
elim [?u].
elim h.
dixi.
argument some_donkey : [?w:Ind] (exists y:Ind, donkey [y]).
elim [?w].
dixi.
argument pd : donkey [pedro].
by default.
dixi.
